Do not charge a page-in to a task that does not exist

VM_PAGE_COUNT_AS_PAGEIN() counts the page-in against the current task, and the
boot thread has no task while the VM comes up, so the counter store faults on
address offsetof(task, pageins).  The macro runs six times in the fault path,
and the first of them is in vm_fault_enter_prepare(), right where the fault
that run-138 died on was being handled: the counter at the top of
vm_fault_internal() was the first of these, and this one is the next.

Charge the task only when there is one.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/vm/vm_page.h b/osfmk/vm/vm_page.h
--- a/osfmk/vm/vm_page.h
+++ b/osfmk/vm/vm_page.h
@@ -1820,9 +1820,17 @@
 	MACRO_BEGIN                                             \
 	{                                                       \
 	vm_object_t o;                                          \
+	task_t pio_task = current_task();                        \
 	o = VM_PAGE_OBJECT(mem);                                \
 	DTRACE_VM2(pgin, int, 1, (uint64_t *), NULL);           \
-	counter_inc(&current_task()->pageins);                  \
+	/*                                                      \
+	 * nio: the boot thread has no task while the VM comes  \
+	 * up, so charging the page-in to it would fault on     \
+	 * address offsetof(task, pageins).                     \
+	 */                                                     \
+	if (pio_task != TASK_NULL) {                             \
+		counter_inc(&pio_task->pageins);                \
+	}                                                       \
 	if (o->internal) {                                      \
 	        DTRACE_VM2(anonpgin, int, 1, (uint64_t *), NULL);       \
 	} else {                                                \
